•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:ks7g2ycpdnhjdtsn3sfoiqoh2tazwtiwr2emxut3ugourttnnbkadbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxqpubkit 0.18.0 was released on 2026-10-29 from commit dac919c76205061c55c28ab0038897b8305e29c3 with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsàÇgchangedyopubkit's main ruleset requires a branch to be up to date with main before it merges (strict_required_status_checks_policy true), so the tree a pull request tested is the tree main holds after the merge, the CI run on main repeats the pull request's, and tagging a release needs no tests of its own; `pubkit protect --check` reports a repository whose ruleset does notÇhinternaly¿The nightly pushes and opens its pull requests as the Sustenaut nightly GitHub App (NIGHTLY_APP_ID, NIGHTLY_APP_KEY): one token per governed repository, for it alone, with contents, pull-requests and workflows write and actions read, from actions/create-github-app-token. A fine-grained token covers one owner only, and the governed repositories moved to the Sustenaut organization. Without the app it falls back to PUBKIT_BUMP_TOKEN with a warningÇefixedypubkit bump and the nightly's pubkit pins move every hand-written use of one of pubkit's actions (<owner>/pubkit/actions/<name>@<commit> # vX.Y.Z or @vX.Y.Z, under Sustenaut or the old schryer), such as deploy-static, to this pubkit's commit and version, so a repository bumped to 0.17.1 no longer runs 0.17.0's site check. pubkit sync --check, and so ci / passed, and pubkit conform fail while such a pin names another pubkit or another commit; one that names no version, such as @main, is left as it is and reportedÇgchangedy`pubkit new` no longer writes an empty corpus/publets/pkg.<name>/unreleased.json: pubrel 0.6 records each unreleased change in a file of its own under unreleased/, and a new package needs pubrel 0.6.0 on this machine; new packages' CI calls pubrel 0.6.0's release workflowÇhinternalx©pubkit's own CI runs pubrel 0.6.0's release workflow, and its unreleased changes are files under corpus/publets/pkg.pubkit/unreleased/; the empty unreleased.json is goneÇeaddedyA repository that deploys a static site with deploy-static gets a ci / site job in its generated pr.yml, part of ci / passed: it builds the site (pubkit.json's new site.pr_build, else site.build) and runs deploy-static at the locked pubkit with its new check-only input, which runs pubkit site check and deploys nothing, so a site that would fail to deploy fails the pull request. site.check_dir names the directory (else the dir the deploy workflow gives deploy-static) and site.url the address; sync refuses any other site settingÇeaddedyÕactions/deploy-ssh deploys by running one command on a server over SSH, with a key the server pins to one program (a forced command reading SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND), a required pinned host key, an optional bundle of workspace paths sent as a gzipped tar on the command's standard input, and an optional tailnet to join first (tailscale/github-action, as tag:ci), for what is not a directory of static files: a service the server rebuilds, a unit of a deploy scriptÇeaddedx÷pubkit cache and actions/cache: keep a build's slow-changing inputs for a period and its per-unit outputs under a fingerprint of what made them, by rules in pubkit.json's cache block (pubkit cache plan, run, prune)gdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:wp6klciged4ygpwhflt6v2k7u2jd5nlkawodxux6szktwgn7szyahevidenceÅ§dkindhexternalcreffpubkithrevisionx(dac919c76205061c55c28ab0038897b8305e29c3drolefsourcedlangbenescope¢jconditionsÄfdomainx'the published release v0.18.0 of pubkitgcreatedt2026-10-29T00:00:00Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose